      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Fertile Wabash River valley soils, mainly Miami silt loam, made the area ideal for corn and wheat farming.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12,
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/parkers_settlement_indiana",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Early residents practiced log\u2011raising and husking\u2011bees, relying on communal labor to build homes and harvest crops.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
